Just following up, the issue has been resolved. It was an initial values issue. My gamma's were too high, leading to a p == 1 in the dbinom of surveys, which resulted in issues when  N != y.

On Thursday, February 2, 2023 at 11:11:38 AM UTC-5 Matthew Gonnerman wrote:
