Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Debbie, good find.  It appears this might be a bug in how the nimble compiler handles the different arguments to the seq (or, the nimSeq) function.

Until we get this sorted, it looks like if you specify the default value of tau=1 into your seq() function, it will clear this problem up:

time <- seq(0,num.days,1)

This doesn't let you specify different values of tau, but please hold tight while this matter is looked into..

Also, you will need to add the returnType(...) statement to the body of your run function:

    }
      returnType(double(1))
    return(traj[-1,])
  })

Thanks for the bug report, and your patience,
Daniel

