MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi Debbie,

Yikes, it does turn out this very simple call to seq has tripped a hidden bug.

A workaround is to avoid having *both* 'from' and 'to' be typed as integers.  E.g., if you do 'num.days = double()', the code should compile.

If you will be calling this function from a model, or passing model variables to it, you should use all double types anyway (especially for the vectors), even when the values will in fact be integers.  (I suspect that's why a bug handling such a simple case could still have gone undetected for so long.)

I'll file an issue for us to fix the bug.

Perry

